1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,830
DRIZZLE: That's... the last jug?

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,600
PREVIOUSLY: DAY 4

3
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:09,440
A working camp. A secret. A list in Gord's tent.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,610
Five days. No rain. The sky forgot how.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,500
Two days of water. Two hundred five people.

6
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,910
[GORD PIKE] GORD: Workers get full rations. That's fair.

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,630
[DARLA FINCH] DARLA: My kids can't haul water!

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,990
GORD: Then they get half.

9
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,210
MAGS: Ration food. Never water.

10
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:45,730
MAGS: Drink what you need. Then go find more.

11
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:52,900
RATION FOOD, NOT WATER. DRINK WHAT YOU NEED.

12
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,800
DRIZZLE: Benny? Whoa, sit.

13
00:00:56,920 --> 00:01:00,640
MAGS: Dizzy. Headache. He's dried out.

14
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:06,160
DEHYDRATION: THIRST, DARK URINE, DIZZINESS, HEADACHE

15
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,650
MAGS: Safe water. Salt and sugar.

16
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:13,380
MAGS: Mixed by a trusted recipe. Not a guess.

17
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,660
MAGS: The creek. Now.

18
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:20,800
DRIZZLE: That's not a creek. That's a leak.

19
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,260
MAGS: It's water. That's what matters.

20
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:30,330
MAGS: Not yet. It looks clean. It isn't.

21
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:33,860
MAGS: Boil it or treat it. Every time.

22
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:40,980
CREEK WATER: BOIL OR TREAT IT, EVEN IF IT LOOKS CLEAN

23
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,610
Twenty minutes. One jug.

24
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,620
DARLA: The Army's at the bridge! Buses!

25
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:57,110
DARLA: Buses at noon. Everyone's going!

26
00:01:58,500 --> 00:01:59,520
MAGS: Who said?

27
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,790
DARLA: Somebody heard it on the radio.

28
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,990
MAGS: Then we wait for the radio.

29
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:12,270
Twenty people waited for a bus that was never coming.

30
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,990
DRIZZLE: There's no road for a bus.

31
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,750
RADIO: ...no evacuation is scheduled... for Gull Harbor...

32
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,790
RADIO: ...remain where you are... await instructions...

33
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:33,900
RUMORS: WAIT FOR AN OFFICIAL SOURCE BEFORE YOU ACT

34
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,790
DRIZZLE: Mags... the tide's out.

35
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:40,510
DRIZZLE: Soup! Beans! Dinner!

36
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:43,560
MAGS: Floodwater touched those.

37
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:48,770
MAGS: Only sealed cans. No dents. Wash them first.

38
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:55,900
FLOODWATER FOOD: THROW IT OUT. ONLY UNDAMAGED CANS CAN BE CLEANED.

39
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,690
DRIZZLE: Goodbye, beans. I barely knew you.

40
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:03,300
DRIZZLE: Found a whistle!

41
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,320
MAGS: Keep it. Somebody'll need it.

42
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:13,780
It was a long walk home. Uphill. With all of it.

43
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,350
MAGS: I'm fine. Keep walking.

44
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,520
DRIZZLE: Mags!

45
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,660
MAGS: Knee. It's the knee.

46
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,890
DRIZZLE: Stop. Don't stand on it.

47
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:35,100
INJURED KNEE: STOP. SUPPORT IT. SHARE THE LOAD.

48
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:38,350
DRIZZLE: Arm over me. I've got the water.

49
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:47,960
For nine days Mags had carried everyone. Now somebody carried her.

50
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:56,380
DRIZZLE: Is that... Hank? With a pack?

51
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:02,020
[HANK DORSEY] HANK: No offense. I'm not dying on a hill for a clipboard.

52
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,250
DRIZZLE: Then don't go alone.

53
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,080
HANK: Nobody's coming with me.

54
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:11,300
DRIZZLE: Then write your route. And when you'll be back.

55
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:16,500
HANK: Highway 4. East. Three days.

56
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,770
DRIZZLE: Three blasts if you're in trouble.

57
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:24,900
NEVER TRAVEL ALONE. LEAVE YOUR ROUTE AND RETURN TIME.

58
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:29,700
He walked into the hills with a whistle and a promise.

59
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,080
DRIZZLE: Day twelve, Hank. I'm counting.

60
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,880
DRIZZLE: Wes. Listen.

61
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:50,900
THREE BLASTS = DISTRESS

62
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:52,600
DRIZZLE: HANK?!

63
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:59,820
Three blasts. Then nothing.
